From 934957297b111682ca483c3f6ada9543f538b1e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:14:53 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Sharp text: the font's text drawn again at the internal
 resolution

sceFontGetCharGlyphImage gives the host a buffer and a position, and the
host draws one glyph into it at the PSP's size. A game may then draw that
buffer as a texture, as Dissidia 012 does with each block of text (4-bit,
about 20-pixel glyphs, drawn at about 0.6 of their size): at 4x the
glyphs were only enlarged, and looked soft.

- fonts/sharp_text: each glyph drawn into a buffer is kept (character,
  position, clip rectangle) with a copy of the buffer as it left it. A
  buffer found clear starts a new text; one the game wrote itself, or one
  drawn with another font, is never drawn sharp.
- fonts::render_scaled(): a glyph drawn factor times as large, with the
  same outline, position and emboldening as the 1x one.
- The renderer: a 4- or 8-bit texture lying in such a buffer, which holds
  exactly what its glyphs left, is drawn as large as the internal
  resolution (up to 8 times, 4096 pixels a side), its glyphs coloured
  through the game's palette and the rest the game's texels; the larger
  picture keeps the texture coordinates, as a texture pack's image does.
  Decided while recording, from guest memory as the draw reads it; the
  game's memory is only read.
- A GPU memory budget of its own (<PREFIX>_SHARP_TEXT_MEMORY=<MB>, 256):
  sharp text not drawn in the last two frames goes first, else the new
  text is drawn from the game's texture, so a screen with more text than
  the budget does not draw it again every frame.
- Settings: text.sharp (on), the Sharp text row in the Video page's Text
  section, restored with the page's defaults; a change, or a new internal
  resolution, draws the text again. <PREFIX>_NO_SHARP_TEXT=1 turns it off
  for a comparison, <PREFIX>_TRACE_SHARP_TEXT=1 logs each lookup.
- gpu::clut_color(): a palette entry as decode_texture() reads it.
- docs/PROFILE_GUIDE.md: a profile needs nothing for it.

Tested on Windows (clang, llvm-mingw) with Dissidia 012 (ULUS10566), test
data only: the first-run Data Config screen, the menus to Quick Battle
Player Select and its "Play as this character?" dialog, Battle Setup and
a Quick Battle at 4x, with and without <PREFIX>_NO_SHARP_TEXT; at 2x; with
Arial as the font; with text.sharp=0; with a 16 MB budget. Every text
texture on those routes was drawn sharp (145 on the menus, 334 with the
battle), none fell back; the battle ran at 60 fps with the same render
time either way. The port's tests pass. Not tested: the menu row while
playing, text drawn letter by letter, Japanese text, Linux, Android, the
framework's own build and tests, another game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
